# Vendored dependencies are somebody else's code, checked in so the build
# needs no network. Reviewing them is not the point of a pull request, and a
# dependency update that touches two hundred files buries the one file the
# change is actually about.
#
# linguist-vendored keeps them out of the repository's language statistics and
# collapses them in a pull request on GitHub, where they stay one click away.
# -diff is the same idea locally: git reports that the file differs rather
# than printing it. Pass --text to git diff to see it anyway.
vendor/** linguist-vendored
vendor/** -diff
